{"bounds": [], "data": {"programs": [{"error": null, "id": "tower_arcs", "instance": {"bind": {"attn0": "live:blocks.0.attn.weights.act", "attn1": "live:blocks.1.attn.weights.act"}, "common": "// lib module colormap@1 (design/programmable-graphics.md, Lib Modules): the\n// host's colormaps. A piece that imports it calls colormap::sample,\n// colormap::viridis or colormap::magma. Released; never changes.\n\n// The rows of caliper_colormaps.\nconst colormap__VIRIDIS: u32 = 0u;\nconst colormap__MAGMA: u32 = 1u;\nconst colormap__RDBU: u32 = 2u;\nconst colormap__GREYS: u32 = 3u;\n\n// The color of t, from 0 to 1, on a host colormap, linear between its texels.\nfn colormap__sample(map: u32, t: f32) -> vec4<f32> {\n    let size = textureDimensions(caliper_colormaps);\n    let row = i32(min(map, size.y - 1u));\n    let x = clamp(t, 0.0, 1.0) * f32(size.x - 1u);\n    let x0 = i32(floor(x));\n    let x1 = min(x0 + 1, i32(size.x) - 1);\n    let a = textureLoad(caliper_colormaps, vec2<i32>(x0, row), 0);\n    let b = textureLoad(caliper_colormaps, vec2<i32>(x1, row), 0);\n    return mix(a, b, x - f32(x0));\n}\n\nfn colormap__viridis(t: f32) -> vec4<f32> {\n    return colormap__sample(colormap__VIRIDIS, t);\n}\n\nfn colormap__magma(t: f32) -> vec4<f32> {\n    return colormap__sample(colormap__MAGMA, t);\n}\n// lib module pick@1 (design/programmable-graphics.md, Lib Modules): the ID\n// that a pick pass writes and the linked selection. A piece that imports it\n// calls pick::id, pick::selected and pick::selected_index. Released; never\n// changes.\n\n// The ID that a pass with pick = true writes at location 1: the program's\n// pick id and the item, an element index of the item map's resource.\nfn pick__id(item: u32) -> vec2<u32> {\n    return vec2<u32>(caliper_view.frame.z, item);\n}\n\n// The count of valid entries of caliper_selection.\nfn pick__selection_count() -> u32 {\n    return min(caliper_view.frame.w, min(arrayLength(&caliper_selection), 256u));\n}\n\n// Whether an item of this program is in the linked selection.\nfn pick__selected(item: u32) -> bool {\n    let n = pick__selection_count();\n    for (var i = 0u; i < n; i = i + 1u) {\n        let s = caliper_selection[i];\n        if (s.pick == caliper_view.frame.z && s.item == item) {\n            return true;\n        }\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n\n// Whether a selected item of any program has these tensor indices; an index\n// below 0 matches every index.\nfn pick__selected_index(index: vec4<i32>) -> bool {\n    let n = pick__selection_count();\n    for (var i = 0u; i < n; i = i + 1u) {\n        let s = caliper_selection[i].index;\n        if (all((index == s) | (index < vec4<i32>(0)))) {\n            return true;\n        }\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n// lib module camera@1 (design/programmable-graphics.md, Lib Modules): clip\n// positions and offsets in pixels from the host camera. A piece that imports\n// it calls camera::clip, camera::pixel_direction and camera::offset_pixels.\n// Released; never changes.\n\n// The clip position of a world position.\nfn camera__clip(world: vec3<f32>) -> vec4<f32> {\n    return caliper_view.clip_from_world * vec4<f32>(world, 1.0);\n}\n\n// The unit direction in pixels from clip position a to clip position b, or\n// (1, 0) when they fall on one pixel.\nfn camera__pixel_direction(a: vec4<f32>, b: vec4<f32>) -> vec2<f32> {\n    let d = (b.xy / b.w - a.xy / a.w) * caliper_view.viewport.zw;\n    let n = length(d);\n    if (n < 1e-6) {\n        return vec2<f32>(1.0, 0.0);\n    }\n    return d / n;\n}\n\n// A clip position moved by a distance in pixels on the screen.\nfn camera__offset_pixels(clip: vec4<f32>, pixels: vec2<f32>) -> vec4<f32> {\n    return clip + vec4<f32>(pixels * 2.0 / caliper_view.viewport.zw * clip.w, 0.0, 0.0);\n}\n// The sizes of the model and of its fixed sentence, which both halves read.\nconst L: u32 = 2u;     // layers\nconst H: u32 = 4u;     // heads\nconst T: u32 = 32u;    // tokens of the fixed sentence\nconst P: u32 = 12u;    // length of the repeated segment\nconst S: u32 = 4u;     // first token of its first copy\n\n// The tower: one ring of tokens for each layer, RISE apart, the lowest at BASE. The host frames\n// a panel of programs alone on the box from -1 to 1, thus a tower of this size fills the panel.\nconst R: f32 = 1.45;      // the radius of a ring\nconst BASE: f32 = -0.85;  // the height of the ring of layer 0\nconst RISE: f32 = 1.5;    // the height from one ring to the next\n\n// The place of a token on the ring of a layer.\nfn ring_point(layer: u32, token: u32) -> vec3<f32> {\n    let a = 6.2831853 * f32(token) / f32(T);\n    return vec3<f32>(R * cos(a), BASE + f32(layer) * RISE, R * sin(a));\n}\n", "derive": "// The weight of a query token i on a key token j, in batch row 0 of the (B, H, T, T) weights,\n// which the script publishes as (B * H * T, T) rows; the first H * T * T values are that row.\nfn attn(layer: u32, head: u32, i: u32, j: u32) -> f32 {\n    let k = (head * T + i) * T + j;\n    if (layer == 0u) {\n        return attn0[k];\n    }\n    return attn1[k];\n}\n\n// The induction score of each head: its mean weight from a token of the\n// second copy to the token after the same token's first occurrence.\n@compute @workgroup_size(8)\nfn scores(@builtin(global_invocation_id) id: vec3<u32>) {\n    if (id.x >= L * H) {\n        return;\n    }\n    var sum = 0.0;\n    for (var t = S + P; t < S + 2u * P; t = t + 1u) {\n        sum = sum + attn(id.x / H, id.x % H, t, t - P + 1u);\n    }\n    heads[id.x] = sum / f32(P);\n}\n\n// One arc for each weight above the threshold, from the key token to the query token.\n@compute @workgroup_size(64)\nfn build(@builtin(global_invocation_id) id: vec3<u32>) {\n    if (id.x >= L * H * T * T) {\n        return;\n    }\n    let j = id.x % T;\n    let i = (id.x / T) % T;\n    let head = (id.x / (T * T)) % H;\n    let layer = id.x / (T * T * H);\n    if (j >= i) {\n        return;                            // causal, and no arc to itself\n    }\n    let w = attn(layer, head, i, j);\n    if (w < params.threshold) {\n        return;\n    }\n    let slot = atomicAdd(&arcs_count, 1u);\n    if (slot >= arrayLength(&arcs)) {\n        return;\n    }\n    arcs[slot] = Arc(j, i, layer, head, w, heads[layer * H + head]);\n}\n\n// One label anchor for each token, just outside the lower ring.\n@compute @workgroup_size(32)\nfn place_labels(@builtin(global_invocation_id) id: vec3<u32>) {\n    if (id.x >= T) {\n        return;\n    }\n    labels[id.x] = Label(vec4<f32>(ring_point(0u, id.x) * 1.15, 1.0), id.x);\n}\n", "draw": "const SEG: u32 = 32u;    // segments of one arc: 64 vertices of a strip\n\nstruct ArcOut {\n    @builtin(position) position: vec4<f32>,\n    @location(0) color: vec4<f32>,\n    @location(1) @interpolate(flat) item: u32,\n}\n\n// The color of each head of a layer, four hues that stay apart when arcs add up.\nfn head_color(head: u32) -> vec3<f32> {\n    var colors = array<vec3<f32>, 4>(vec3<f32>(1.0, 0.55, 0.2), vec3<f32>(0.25, 0.75, 1.0),\n                                     vec3<f32>(0.85, 0.4, 1.0), vec3<f32>(0.45, 0.95, 0.45));\n    return colors[head % 4u];\n}\n\n// A point of the arc's quadratic curve, raised above its ring by its weight, and by its head, so\n// that the same token pair of four heads gives four arcs and not one.\nfn arc_point(arc: Arc, t: f32) -> vec3<f32> {\n    let p0 = ring_point(arc.layer, arc.from_token);\n    let p2 = ring_point(arc.layer, arc.to_token);\n    let lift = 0.08 + 0.45 * arc.weight + 0.12 * f32(arc.head);\n    let p1 = 0.5 * (p0 + p2) + vec3<f32>(0.0, lift, 0.0);\n    let u = 1.0 - t;\n    return u * u * p0 + 2.0 * u * t * p1 + t * t * p2;\n}\n\n// A strip along the arc, of a width in pixels that grows with the weight, colored by the head. A\n// weak weight gives a faint arc and a strong one a bright arc, below white even where a few add up.\n@vertex\nfn arc_vs(@builtin(instance_index) i: u32, @builtin(vertex_index) v: u32) -> ArcOut {\n    let arc = arcs[i];\n    let t = f32(v / 2u) / f32(SEG - 1u);\n    let e = 0.5 / f32(SEG - 1u);\n    let c = camera__clip(arc_point(arc, t));\n    let a = camera__clip(arc_point(arc, max(t - e, 0.0)));\n    let b = camera__clip(arc_point(arc, min(t + e, 1.0)));\n    let d = camera__pixel_direction(a, b);\n    let side = f32(v % 2u) - 0.5;\n    let selected = pick__selected(i);\n    var width = (1.0 + 2.5 * arc.weight) * caliper_view.time.z;\n    if (selected) {\n        width = width * 1.6;\n    }\n    var out: ArcOut;\n    out.position = camera__offset_pixels(c, vec2<f32>(-d.y, d.x) * side * width);\n    // Fainter towards the ends, where the arcs of one token meet and would add up to white.\n    let taper = 0.3 + 0.7 * sin(3.14159265 * t);\n    let k = (0.025 + 0.28 * arc.weight * arc.weight) * taper;\n    out.color = vec4<f32>(head_color(arc.head) * k, k);\n    out.item = i;\n    if (selected) {\n        out.color = vec4<f32>(1.0, 0.9, 0.6, 1.0);\n    }\n    return out;\n}\n\n@fragment\nfn arc_fs(in: ArcOut) -> CaliperPicked {\n    var out: CaliperPicked;\n    out.color = in.color;\n    out.id = pick__id(in.item);\n    return out;\n}\n\n@fragment\nfn arc_glow(in: ArcOut) -> @location(0) vec4<f32> {\n    return in.color;\n}\n\n// A Gaussian blur of the half-size glow target, added over the arcs.\n@fragment\nfn bloom(in: CaliperFullscreen) -> @location(0) vec4<f32> {\n    let texel = 1.0 / vec2<f32>(textureDimensions(glow));\n    var sum = vec4<f32>(0.0);\n    for (var y = -2; y <= 2; y = y + 1) {\n        for (var x = -2; x <= 2; x = x + 1) {\n            let w = exp(-f32(x * x + y * y) / 4.0);\n            let uv = in.uv + vec2<f32>(f32(x), f32(y)) * texel * 2.0;\n            sum = sum + w * textureSampleLevel(glow, caliper_linear, uv, 0.0);\n        }\n    }\n    return sum * 0.03 * params.glow;\n}\n", "id": "tower_arcs", "manifest": {"derive": {"passes": [{"entry": "scores", "writes": ["heads"]}, {"entry": "build", "workgroups": [128, 1, 1], "writes": ["arcs"]}, {"entry": "place_labels"}]}, "description": "Arcs between the tokens of one sentence, one ring for each layer, from the attention weights", "draw": {"passes": [{"blend": "additive", "depth": "none", "fragment": "arc_fs", "instances": "arcs", "kind": "render", "pick": true, "topology": "triangle_strip", "vertex": "arc_vs", "vertices": 64}, {"fragment": "arc_glow", "instances": "arcs", "kind": "render", "target": "glow", "topology": "triangle_strip", "vertex": "arc_vs", "vertices": 64}, {"blend": "additive", "fragment": "bloom", "kind": "render", "reads": ["glow"]}], "pick": {"fields": ["layer", "head", "from_token", "to_token", "weight", "score"], "resource": "arcs"}, "targets": [{"id": "glow", "scale": 0.5}], "text": {"anchors": "labels", "strings": ["the", "old", "map", "shows", "red", "fox", "jumps", "over", "lazy", "dogs", "near", "green", "hills", "under", "blue", "skies", "red", "fox", "jumps", "over", "lazy", "dogs", "near", "green", "hills", "under", "blue", "skies", "and", "then", "it", "ends"]}}, "imports": ["colormap@1", "pick@1", "camera@1"], "inputs": [{"kind": "tensor", "name": "attn0", "rank_max": 2, "rank_min": 2, "title": "Attention Weights of Layer 0"}, {"kind": "tensor", "name": "attn1", "rank_max": 2, "rank_min": 2, "title": "Attention Weights of Layer 1"}], "name": "attention_arcs", "params": [{"default": 0.05, "max": 0.5, "min": 0, "name": "threshold", "title": "Weight Threshold"}, {"default": 1, "max": 4, "min": 0, "name": "glow", "title": "Glow"}], "resources": [{"count": 8, "element": "f32", "id": "heads", "kind": "buffer"}, {"count": 4096, "counted": true, "fields": ["from_token: u32", "to_token: u32", "layer: u32", "head: u32", "weight: f32", "score: f32"], "id": "arcs", "kind": "buffer", "struct": "Arc"}, {"count": 32, "fields": ["position: vec4<f32>", "string: u32"], "id": "labels", "kind": "buffer", "struct": "Label"}], "version": 1}, "op": "set", "panel": "tower", "params": {"threshold": 0.05}, "piece": {"hash": "sha256:1e756ab8592359